@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# Original payment receipt customer publication · UNAPPLIED
+
+Isolated child of #478 `28f98e6f58f3ac02518efed33a8946eb9537f005`. No parent bytes are changed. This is a concrete default-OFF SQL/reader/renderer candidate; no operational route, link, sender, credentials, customer grant or hosted installation exists.
+
+The new private `commercial_payment_access` table is a bounded **authorization mapping only**. It stores no amount, balance, provider transaction or second business ledger. A grant binds purpose, tenant/customer/location/current portal user, exact issued invoice/source/revision/original issuance command, existing merchant/original attempt and the digest of the immutable stored gateway result. Grant/revoke authority needs current staff MFA, the unchanged publisher guard and an independently approved dedicated merchant workload. No runtime LOGIN principal or customer/publisher EXECUTE grant is supplied. Only finite helper execution is granted to the private NOLOGIN owner. Protected-source admission, installer/function-owner/runtime grants and capability changes require separate exact approval.
+
+Grant creation reuses #476's original capture/refund reader and accepts only a successful immutable gateway outcome. Pending, UNKNOWN and declined rows cannot become customer receipts. Staff creator status reads recover the exact original publication acknowledgment without another grant or payment. Mapping rows can only be revoked, never rebound/extended/deleted. The original financial records remain unchanged. Rollback/restore resistance and independent one-use write custody remain D2 acceptance requirements; this mapping does not provide them.
+
+Customer reads use the original `customer_portal_guard`, current session/user/active portal mapping and a separate exact commercial grant. AAL2 is retained conservatively. Source currentness uses the exact existing canonical predicate under original estimate/version locks, without calling or weakening the issued-draft guard. Reads recheck current authorization after waits; grant/session expiry withholds the response. The response expires within thirty seconds and never beyond the original grant/JWT/session bound. Cached projections are not instantaneous push revocation; reopening requires a new current read.
+
+Only sandbox evidence is supported. The customer card visibly labels its provenance and separately identifies an issuance reference, original capture/refund reference and recorded amount. The original invoice amount is contextual, **not a balance**. No amount netting, debt, cancellation, dispute, bank/fee/net deposit or verified settlement is inferred. Provider identifiers, idempotency/authorization keys, source hashes, digests, staff identity, sessions, contacts, tokens and private notes never leave the server. Public UUID references are display facts, never authentication or financial execution authority. Full invoice numbering/viewer integration remains separate; this candidate does not bypass the existing UUID-only invoice/customer decoders or the separate #475 numbering/client approval checkpoint.
+
+The unmounted component defaults OFF. Explicit reopen clears prior content before a read; expired/revoked/foreign/stale/UNKNOWN evidence stays hidden. Context replacement, unmount, cancellation, a five-second deadline and equal-time cached observations suppress late content. No customer payment URL, send/resend, financial mutation or operational provider adapter is introduced. `GatewaySql` cancellation/pool discard and genuine bearer-to-database binding remain unqualified; the proposal supplies no connection/Auth factory.
+
+## Verification boundary
+
+New qualification captures the exact parent helper and all original migration/source bytes before returning proposal SQL, and rejects source, symlink, mode and withdrawal substitutions. Native tests use actual existing draft/issuance/capture/refund engines and this SQL in a disposable PostgreSQL cluster. Controlled fixture roles/JWT/Auth rows and explicit local capability/function grants exercise permissions; they are **not genuine hosted Auth or installed customer14 acceptance**. Canonical source/migration files remain unchanged. Both new capability and canonical capabilities remain OFF in source. Fixture role names are file-owned and randomized, with exact CI bootstrap role preparation.
+
+Author results:30 native PASS /0 FAIL /0 SKIP;27 PGlite PASS plus3 explicit native-only observed-wait skips;34 reader +11 source controls PASS;8 desktop/mobile browser PASS /0 skipped/flaky. Browser cases use the actual Node proposed decoder with a controlled rows port and rendered component; they test visibility/accessibility/privacy and do not prove real Auth or hosted SQL. Independent results are reported separately in the draft PR. No accepted #476/#478 suites are rerun.
+
+Two early review findings were reproduced and corrected only in new source: issued-draft projection rejected an issued header (replaced by the exact original source predicate), and opposite publish/revoke lock order produced native40P01 (all grant/status/revoke paths now acquire workload before mapping locks). Sync driver error details are normalized too. Failed development reports and initial Chromium sandbox Mach-port launch failure remain private; later browser execution used explicit local browser approval. No assertion/budget/skip or original protection was weakened.
+
+## Held operational action
+
+The smallest future action is exact-source review/admission of this new private mapping/function/column-grant bundle and separately bound nonproduction principals/target/window. It does not itself authorize execution. Original customer14/source/capability permissions, current genuine customer Auth/MFA/session binding, D1 responsibilities and installed bypass inventory, D2 independent custody/ACK/spent fencing, D3 recovery and original A01–A12 remain mandatory. Customer intake SQL remains HELD. A future approved server bridge must obtain private source/header/issuance anchors from the current grant, never public numbers, URLs or a copied response. No payment publication can be inferred from an estimate grant.
+
+Saul 2 Paul remains first; Cunningham needs separate tenant/customer/Auth/merchant/key/settlement acceptance. VAR/NMI boarding, actual provider reports/fees/deposits/bank evidence and customer delivery remain external gates. No real tenant/invoice/payment, hosted SQL/grant, provider request, communication, merge, deployment or operational recovery occurred. **Release 1.0 NO-GO.**
