@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# Customer publication read-boundary and source-author proposal
+
+Status: development proposal only; default OFF; operationalReady false. Exact parent is #480 `da1e42d5d9c00cc51c60e7e35016bfc1067ce1b7`. No existing file is changed.
+
+The missing boundary in #480 was a qualified caller/SQL connection: its receipt reader alone accepts an injected port. `read-only.ts` now composes the existing opaque `CustomerBrokerAuth` / `CommercialCallerConnection` guard with the unchanged #480 customer receipt reader. It never acquires a connection, creates Auth, changes claims or roles, or provisions a principal. Existing customer publication/access grants remain separately required; neither staff authority, a URL nor an estimate grant supplies commercial customer authority.
+
+A fixed catalog read before and after the receipt requires the same dedicated LOGIN/current role, no memberships or admin/bypass/create/replication flags, explicit direct private-schema USAGE and exact receipt EXECUTE (never PUBLIC fallback, ownership or grant-option delegation), no raw table/column access or schema CREATE, and no other reachable application-schema SECURITY DEFINER function. The existing caller guard rechecks actual backend/claims and the current SDK user/session/AAL2 around every query. Exact source bytes, modes and nonsymlink ancestors are checked before work and after awaits, with the complete relative-source import closure pinned. The five-second total deadline includes Auth. Late revocation, source changes, privilege changes, cancellation and uncertain reads suppress output. Failures retire this injected object without a retry or alternate connection.
+
+These are local checks, not independent operational custody. The trusted host must exclusively own the physical connection; object retirement does not fence aliases, cancel server work, prove pool discard, survive process loss or supply a durable hold. Current catalog snapshots do not prove all installed writers/bypasses, an atomic administrative revocation barrier or function-body identity in a hosted catalog. Static imports execute before these checks: trusted source loading, exact bundle/loader/dependency qualification and installed-source inventory remain separate gates. The pinned lockfile is not a proof of installed dependency bytes. No connection or credential factory is supplied.
+
+## Finite, UNAPPLIED source-author checkpoint
+
+`source-author.patch` SHA256 `f9d63696a6c6731bea3c6384dfc66780650e89ca066e61f222f5139df44cc9ae` adds exactly two mode-100644 source files on #480, copying already reviewed proposal bytes without changing behavior:
+
+- `server/invoices/commercial-payment-receipt.proposed.sql`: SHA256 `1c1ec82ca52560de86ec19ff9a865babfc3967ff466b425692e733fd240fdef5`.
+- `server/invoices/customer-payment-publication.proposed.sql`: SHA256 `bff7f5f16fa620b4f7e684228d1ff41af696492027a782ea4698fe49d1fbb71d`.
+
+Both canonical endpoints remain absent here. The patch is applied only to an owned temporary directory by source tests, never to this candidate or a database. Original manifests and historical pins remain unchanged. There is no checker mutation, launch admission or implicit composition with #479/#482/#483. Unknown path/mode/payload substitutions deny. Source authorship, protected checker admission, launch integration, SQL installation and runtime grants are separate approvals.
+
+`reader-grants.sql.in` is an inactive two-statement template for direct private-schema USAGE and the exact receipt function EXECUTE to an already reviewed dedicated LOGIN. The private target/principal binding, role creation, default PUBLIC grants, installed definer ownership/function bodies/helper grants, writer/bypass inventory, trusted installer and revocation/pool-discard implementation require separate exact review. No runtime LOGIN or customer EXECUTE is created/granted by this proposal. No public role, role membership, table grant, operational capability or customer publication/access grant is supplied.
+
+The next source-only authorization, if desired after independent review, is: **Apply only patch `f9d63696a6c6731bea3c6384dfc66780650e89ca066e61f222f5139df44cc9ae` on an isolated source-author child of exact #480 `da1e42d5d9c00cc51c60e7e35016bfc1067ce1b7`, adding only the two listed mode-100644 SQL source files.** This excludes admission/promotion, SQL or grant installation, hosted Auth/operations, credentials, real tenants/merchants, provider/financial actions, communications, recovery, merges, deployments and activation.
+
+## Qualification and remaining acceptance
+
+Only new controls are run: 28 wrapper/source negatives plus seven finite-package controls, and twelve native PostgreSQL17 read-boundary cases. Native tests connect an actual dedicated restricted LOGIN to a fresh TCP-disabled Unix-socket database. A controlled SDK transport reads fixture Auth/session state; it is not genuine hosted Auth/MFA. Tests cover actual role membership, superuser, column and definer grants, PUBLIC fallback and grant-option delegation denial, post-read privilege change, session revocation and wrong customer. The cluster is stopped and removed. Existing #480 45 unit/source, 30 native and eight browser tests are reused only for their unchanged source; they are not repeated or counted as new coverage. No new UI is added, so no additional browser acceptance is claimed.
+
+The original receipt distinguishes recorded capture/refund from balance and verified settlement; balance remains NOT_ESTABLISHED and settlement UNVERIFIED. Nothing replays a financial mutation, releases UNKNOWN holds or establishes a bank deposit. Genuine current Auth/MFA, reviewed installed SQL/grants and customer access mapping, source/loader/bundle qualification, physical connection custody/discard, D1–D3, original A01–A12 and recovery remain HELD. VAR sheets, separate NMI merchant bindings and provider/bank acceptance remain separate. Saul 2 Paul is first; Cunningham needs independent tenant/customer/merchant acceptance. Release 1.0 remains NO-GO.
+
+Reference: existing session checks are retained; Supabase documents the `session_id` relationship to `auth.sessions` at https://supabase.com/docs/guides/auth/sessions. No SDK or API contract is changed.
